C - IF/ELSE
============

Make decisions in your program.


IF STATEMENT
------------
if (age >= 18) {
    printf("Adult\n");
}

Runs code only if condition is true.


IF-ELSE
-------
if (x > 10) {
    printf("Big\n");
} else {
    printf("Small\n");
}


IF-ELSE IF-ELSE
----------------
if (grade == 'A') {
    printf("Excellent\n");
} else if (grade == 'B') {
    printf("Good\n");
} else {
    printf("Try again\n");
}


COMPARISON OPERATORS
---------------------
==   Equal
!=   Not equal
>    Greater than
<    Less than
>=   Greater or equal
<=   Less or equal


LOGICAL OPERATORS
------------------
&&   AND
||   OR
!    NOT


EXAMPLES
--------
if (x > 0 && x < 10)
    printf("Between 1-9\n");

if (x < 0 || x > 100)
    printf("Out of range\n");


TERNARY OPERATOR
-----------------
int max = (a > b) ? a : b;

Shorthand for if-else.


COMMON ERRORS
-------------
Using = instead of ==
Forgetting && or ||
Condition never true
Logic errors


TIPS
----
Test all branches.
Use braces always.
Comment complex conditions.
Break into functions for clarity.
